    "https://careers.owu.edu/staff/": {
      "title": "Career Connection Team",
      "description": "Career Connection Team - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Career Connection Team Leigh Mascolino Carolyn Lammert Newton Kimberly ’13 Mindy Agin Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Contact 740-368-3150 Slocum Hall Room 211 lemascolin@owu.edu SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT “To inspire confidence in others so that they can grow into their best selves and create a life fulfilled” Leigh oversees the Career Connection office, supervises staff, and provides strategic leadership in the OWU Career Connection program. She provides individualized career coaching to students and establishes rapport with staff, faculty, employers, and Alumni to expand job prospects and graduate/professional opportunities for OWU students. Leigh has a B.A. in Psychology from Ohio State and an M.S./Ed.S. in Career Counseling from Florida State, where she was trained under the Cognitive Information Processing (CIP) theory. She is a Certified Professional Career Coach (CPCC), a Certified Professional Resume Writer (CPRW), National Certified Counselor (NCC), a Certified Strengths Coach, and an MBTI Certified Practitioner. Leigh served as President of the Ohio Career Development Association and has most recently worked as the Manager of Career Services in the College of Pharmacy at Ohio State. ⬆ Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Contact 740-368-3549 Corns 230 ctlammer@owu.edu SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT Economics & Business Career Community To motivate, inspire and prepare students so that they can find joy, success and prosperity in their life’s work” As Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for the Economics and Business Department, Carolyn is responsible for educating students about career resources and connecting them to great internship and job opportunities with the ultimate goal of preparing them for life after OWU! Carolyn has a Bachelor’s Degree in Interpersonal and Public Communication from Bowling Green State University and a Master of Labor and Human Resources from The Ohio State University. She has a wealth of experience in multi-level corporate recruiting, student advising and internship program management. ⬆ Newton Kimberly ’13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & the Arts Contact 740 368-3642 Slocum Hall Room 208 nskimberly@owu.edu @newton-kimberly-iii SCHEDULE AN APPOITMENT Careers with Social Impact Career Community Humanities & Fine Arts Career Community Career Course Instructor “To lift others, support partners, and give people the tools in order to give them control” As a Career Catalyst (Careers with Social Impact), Newton works with students to help connect them to socially charged careers that align with their personal mission. Utilizing the amazing tools in the Career Connection office, Newton creates and maintains connections with students and employers to help ensure quality experiences for students, both pre and post-graduation, as well as quality and qualified candidates for employers. Newton has a Bachelor’s Degree in Sociology from Ohio Wesleyan University and a Master’s Degree in Public Administration from Cleveland State University.  Prior to returning to OWU, Newton worked as an Academic/College Advisor with I Know I Can and as the Development Associate for TECH CORPS. ⬆ Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Contact 740-368-3153 209 Slocum Hall mbagin@owu.edu @mindybagin SCHEDULE AND APPOITMENT “To motivate students so that they grow to be the best versions of themselves, articulate their stories with confidence, and own who they are” Exploratory Career Community Education Career Community Mindy coaches students on internship success strategies, career exploration, and networks with employers to develop internship opportunities. She leads the Bishop Launch Program, an intern development program designed to help students become confident, competent and competitive internship and job seekers. She is available to meet with students of any major. Prior to joining OWU, Mindy worked for 10 years as a Career Strategist in the Career and Workforce Development Program at Jewish Family Services in Columbus, OH. Mindy holds a BA in Judaic Studies and Political Science from Emory University and an MS in Human Resources Management from the New School for Social Research in NYC, NY. Mindy is a Certified Professional Resume Writer and member of the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE). ⬆ Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
