    "https://careers.owu.edu/channels/careers-with-social-impact/": {
      "title": "Careers with Social Impact",
      "description": "Careers with Social Impact - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Careers with Social Impact Are you looking for a career that will enable you to serve others and address tough social problems? In this career community, you can explore opportunities in Law & Social Justice, Human & Social Services, Social Entrepreneurship, Nonprofits, Government, and International Affairs & Public Policy. Careers With Social Impact Case Manager Policy Analyst Grant Administrator Lawyer Community Relations Manager Special Events Coordinator Fundraising Strategist Copywriter – Public & Social Impact Speech Writer Non-Profit Practitioner Care Advocate Psychologist Archaeologist Social Researcher Community Resource Specialist Social Impact Graduate Degrees + Are you interested in obtaining a Graduate Degree? Here are a few tips to help make the process a little bit easier! Do your research: Start by researching what degree would be best for your career trajectory. Connect with Alumni or additional friends/family members who may have the degree you are interested in and ask them about it! Look into any requirements including location, cost, testing required, deadlines, essays, and cost. Get Organized: Create a spreadsheet or additional document detailing all of the schools that you are interested in applying to. Note the school name, the application deadline, any test scores you might need, essays, contact information, assistantships/TA positions, and cost (Note that graduate admissions application fees can not usually be waived and can cost between $0 – $150, depending on the school. Usually they fall in the $50 – $100 range per school). Get Documents Reviewed: Before submitting any personal statement or essay answer, Career Connection recommends at least 2 pairs of eyes on each response. Your Career Catalyst, the Writing Center, Professors, and Supervisors can be great resources to utilize in order to make sure you answer the prompt to the best of your ability.\\ J.D. (Juris Doctor) (Law) + Learn more about what a JD degree is and what to expect from programming here! MA in Gender and Sexuality Studies + Looking to continue with a MA in Gender and Sexuality? While the title of the program can vary, be aware that the construction of the program varies greatly as well! Be sure to check out the components of each degree in addition to cost, value, and additional opportunities here! MPA (Public Administration) + Learn More about what an MPA degree is, career trajectories, and overall ROI here! MSW (Social Work) + Becoming a social worker varies depending on what state you would like to practice in! Learn about programs, find state qualifications, and discover the right program for you here! Ph.D. and Psy.D. (Psychology) + Interested in learning more about the difference between Ph.D. and Psy.D. programs in Psychology? Looking for resources, top schools, and career outcomes? Click here! Social Impact 2026 – 2027 Events + Social Impact Networking Night – Network with professionals in a small, laid back, and casual setting! Have some snacks, mingle with professionals in the Social Impact sphere, Active Application Workshop – Applying for a job can be hard. Join us for this Monthly Active Application Workshop Internship and Graduate School Fair (Thursday, September 17th) – Interested in an internship or attending graduate school? This is the place for you! Join about 30+ graduate schools and 40+ employers! Summer Internship and Job Fair – Join 70+ employers to learn about open summer internships, careers for graduates, and amazing gap year opportunities! Delaware City and County Managers Association – Learn from representatives of the DCMA as they share about their roles in local government and the amazing opportunities in your own backyard! Seeking Alumni in Careers with Social Impact ? Look no further! We have a cultivated list of Alums who are eager to speak with you. Check out their profiles and reach out! Access tools on our Build a Network page for further templates and resources! CAREERS WITH SOCIAL IMPACT ALUMNI PARTNERS We strongly encourage that you create a LinkedIn profile ! This is a great way to build your network and connect with fellow Alumni, faculty, and connections from OWU. Check out 15,000+ OWU Alumni , and join the OWU group below! OWU ALUMNI & FRIENDS GROUP Search JOIN THIS CAREER COMMUNITY! SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT Meet your Career Catalyst Newton Kimberly ’13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Upcoming Events Alumni Partner Meet & Greet – The Art of the Informational Interview (Thursday, September 10th 2026, 7:00 pm – 8:00 pm EDT) July 8, 2026 Featured Jobs Tax Technician 1 or Tax Technician Trainee 1 at NYS Department of Taxation and Finance August 26, 2026 Auditor Trainee (TAX) or Auditor 1 (TAX) (CID) – Erie County (ID222266) (Full Time – On Site Position in Buffalo, NY) at NYS Department of Taxation and Finance August 26, 2026 CYP Child and Youth Program Direct Care Supervisor at Naval Civilian Careers August 12, 2026 Featured Internships Graduate Intern – Implementation Support (ID: 110793) Fall 2026 at NYS Office of Children and Family Services HR Division September 1, 2026 Fundraising and Events Intern – Fall 2026 at OneHope August 27, 2026 Advancement & Donor Relations Intern – Fall 2026 at OneHope August 27, 2026 Templates & Examples Social Impact Resume Sample (Psychology) Check out this Psychology Resume example – download and review. Social Impact Resume Sample (Government) Check out this Government Resume example. OWU Alumni Partners Jai Chabria ’99 Managing Director Sarah Downs ’06 Director of Health Programming and Delivery Grace Egan ’23 Account Executive Megan Forth ’13 Client Relationship Consultant (Banker) Benjamin (Ben) Hammett Walkuski ’07 Director, Individual Engagement & Philanthropy Erika Hankins-Prantil ’11 Senior Project Manager Jerri Harris ’81 Career Development Manager Sean Harris ’97 Attorney/Partner Sarah JanTausch Founder, Career & Executive Coach — Value Based Careers Sarah Kennedy ’18 Program Officer – Open Government Partnership Newton Kimberly ’13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Carrie Reinhardt ’94 Executive Administrator DeLaine Mayer ’12 Head of Sustainability; Adjunct Faculty Mary Kate McElroy ’21, MFA Instructor of Record; MSW Student Jim Mendenhall Director of Philanthropy and Community Engagement Madison Miller ’22 Communications & Marketing Specialist Emma Nuiry ’17 Manager, Talent Acquisition Operations Kelly O’Donnell ’11 Political Action Committee (PAC) Director Alexander Pacilio ’18 Staff Assessment Leader and Student Readiness Teacher Anthony M. Peddle ’14 Assistant Principle Forrest Rilling Communications Director Diana Roach ’72 Kenneth (Ken) Robinson ’95 Regional Disaster Officer Josh Sanders ’97 Partner Dan Sharpe ’06 Vice President Mark Shipps ’70 Environmental Services (Retired) Andrew Sloan ’13 Director of Development Leon Smith ’95 Executive Director Anna VanMeter Outpatient Psychologist Rachel Vinciguerra ’14 Vice President of Programs Evelyn Walter Founder and Coach Zach Weaver ’11 Corporate Strategy Consultant Laura Weichel Quality Improvement Coordinator Shondra E. Wygal ’94 Associate State Director, Outreach & Advocacy Career Resources & Job Boards Student Assistantship Program (StAP) Discover on-campus paid internships. Legacy Internships Discover on-campus paid internships for Legacy Students. First Gen Internship Discover on-campus paid internships for First Gen Students. NACE Competency Self-Assessment Are you career-ready? Discover more through this self-assessment tool. Exploratory Guide Exploratory Guide OWU Career Connection Overview Brochure/ Guide An introduction to OWU’s most important resource- Career Connection! 1 2 3 4 >> OWU Student Organizations Citizens of the World House (SLU) The Citizens of the World House, a Small Living Unit at Ohio Wesleyan University, was founded in 2009, with the mission of creating a community where students from diverse cultural backgrounds could live with each other in a supportive and open world of cross-cultural experiences that promote understanding and curiosity about our globe. Circle K Circle K International (CKI) is one of the world’s largest student-led collegiate service organizations, with thousands of members on hundreds of campuses across the globe. \n\n\nThe collegiate branch of the Kiwanis International family, CKI is committed to developing leaders by offering unique service, leadership and fellowship opportunities that change the world and the lives of our members. \n\n\nCKI ... Black Student Union We welcome you to join but also stand with us in our mission: 1) To build a cohesive bond among the Black student community at Ohio Wesleyan University, 2)To promote social, cultural, and political awareness of African-American issues, and 3) To help provide members with knowledge about themselves as well as Black culture as a ... Rafiki Wa Africa The purpose of this organization is to raise awareness of African and Caribbean cultures while creating an environment for people of all backgrounds to connect. We aim to connect people of different heritages, and educate the wider Ohio Wesleyan community through educational presentations, and signature events throughout the semester. Our events will be ways for ... House of Black Culture (SLU) The Butler A. Jones House of Black Culture is a residence that houses 10 students. The house is named for former sociology professor Butler A. Jones, known for his work with race relations and the Civil Rights Movement. The House of Black Culture has played a significant part in campus history and continues to serve ... OWU Faith and Justice OWU Faith and Justice is a group dedicated to pursuing justice through the lens of the Christian faith and exploring justice issues from the perspective of other traditions and religions. We aim to understand issues that impact the world around us, from our neighbors on campus to our neighbors around the globe. We meet regularly ... Match Major Sheets Major Sheet: Psychology Match Major Sheet: Sociology-Anthropology Match Major Sheet: Sociology-Anthropology Match Major Sheet: Pre-Law Match Major Sheet: Pre-Law Match Major Sheet: Religious Studies Match Major Sheet: Religious Studies Match Major Sheet: Social Justice Match Major Sheet: Social Justice Featured Jobs Tax Technician 1 or Tax Technician Trainee 1 at NYS Department of Taxation and Finance Employer: NYS Department of Taxation and Finance