es: 09/12/2026 OneHope is a global ministry that seeks to catalyze a movement to help every child in every generation encounter Jesus through engagement with God's Word. By working with local churches, international ministry partners, schools, and governments, […] Gain Experience People In Need Internships 📍Delaware, OH, United States\n\n\n\nSponsor: People in Need\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPeople In Need, Inc. of Delaware County Ohio (PIN) is a private, not-for-profit 501(C)(3) social services agency dedicated to providing emergency assistance to Delaware County residents.\n\n\nOur Mission: Providing relief to our neighbors in their time of need.\n\n\nPrograms include Food Insecurity, Emergency Services, Holiday Clearing House, and the School Shoes ... Academy for Civic Education and Democracy 📍Washington, DC, United States\n\n\n\nSponsor: Ronald Reagan Institute\n\n\n\n\nApply by: Jan 15, 2027\n\n\n\nThe Academy for Civic Education and Democracy (ACED) will convene a new cohort in June of the Summer Semester. ACED is the Ronald Reagan Institute’s in-person bipartisan 8-week summer program in Washington, DC. Classes will be held at the Ronald Reagan Institute building and are ... Greif Internships & Early Career Development 📍Delaware, OH, United States\n\n\n\nSponsor: Greif\n\n\n\n\nApply by: Oct 1, 2026\n\n\n\nAt Greif, we understand the value of cultivating a pipeline of talented individuals at the beginning of their professional journey. As such, Greif facilitates a number of Early Career programs to encourage growth & development through our Internship & Co-Op opportunities. Our Early Career Program in the ... Summer on the Cuyahoga (SOTC) 📍OH, United States\n\n\n\nSponsor: Summer on the Cuyahoga \n\n\n\n\nApply by: Nov 1, 2026\n\n\n\nUnforgettable Summer Internship Experiences are Made in Cleveland!\n\n\nSummer on the Cuyahoga (SOTC) connects young talent with professional opportunities in Northeast Ohio. The program immerses 70-80 students in the Cleveland area, in challenging internships with over 40 employers in a wide variety ... Ohio Department of Natural Resources Summer Internships 📍OH, United States\n\n\n\nSponsor: Ohio Department of Natural Resources\n\n\n\n\nApply by: Nov 1, 2026\n\n\n\nODNR offers hands-on, mission-driven summer internships across Ohio, giving students the chance to explore careers in conservation, science, education, law enforcement, communications, and more. Interns play a direct role in protecting Ohio’s natural resources — including forests, rivers, wildlife, and geological features — while ... Professional Associations PASS: Prevention Awareness Support Services PASS: Prevention Awareness Support Services American Anthropological Association American Anthropological Association Archaeological Institute of America Archaeological Institute of America National Women’s Studies Association National Women's Studies Association Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
