    "https://careers.owu.edu/channels/employers/": {
      "title": "Employers",
      "description": "Employers - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Employers WELCOME EMPLOYERS! Career Connection welcomes your participation in recruiting OWU students. Recognized as a leading national liberal arts university by U.S. News & World Report , Ohio Wesleyan University offers a high-quality liberal arts education in an atmosphere that fosters learning, growth, service, and excellence. Ohio Wesleyan’s students are not only prepared to contribute critical thinking, effective communication, and leadership skills to your organization, but also a civic understanding and international appreciation. Career Connection offers two robust career fairs a year with 70+ employers and programs. Registration is on Handshake, and we typically have 250+ students attend our events. We are excited to welcome you to OWU’s campus in Delaware, OH! Reach out to careers@owu.edu with questions and to express your interest. Attend our upcoming Career Fair : OWU Career & Grad School Fair September 17, 2026 | 11:00am – 2pm Please join us for the annual OWU Career & Grad School Fair in September. We welcome employers seeking full-time and/or part-time employees, as well as graduate/professional schools interested in gaining visibility among a bright and talented group of students. EMPLOYERS REGISTER HERE! Campus Map *If you don’t already have a Handshake Employer Account , please do so first. Questions? Email Leigh Mascolino, Director of Career Connection, or call 740-368-3150. See other fantastic opportunities below : Career & Grad School Fair – September 17, 2026 + Please join us for the annual OWU Career & Grad School Fair in September. We welcome employers seeking full-time and/or part-time employees, as well as graduate/professional schools interested in gaining visibility among a bright and talented group of students. *If you do not already have a Handshake Employer Account , please create one first and add yourself as a contact. Questions? Email Leigh Mascolino, Director of Career Connection, at lemascolin@owu.edu or call 740-368-3150. Career & Summer Internship Fair + February 26, 2026 | 11:30am – 2pm Ohio Wesleyan University invites you to participate in our annual Career & Summer Internship Fair in the Benes Room of the Hamilton-Williams Campus Center. This event is now part of the larger OWU Connection Conference . The OWU Career & Summer Internship Fair is suited for employers who are seeking to hire full-time, part-time, interns, and/or seasonal employees. This event offers a valuable platform for all students to learn about your organization and opportunities. We look forward to seeing you in person at the fair! Campus Map *If you don’t already have a Handshake Employer Account , please do so first. Questions? Email Leigh Mascolino, Director of Career Connection, or call 740-368-3150. Post a Position on Handshake or Newsletter + 1). Handshake Job Board: Handshake allows prospective employers to post jobs and internships and search student resumes. If you are specifically seeking Ohio Wesleyan students or alumni, you can post directly on Handshake . If you need assistance, access the Handshake Help Center and see more about how to Register as an Employer on Handshake . 2). Include in a Bi-Weekly Newsletter: Our Career Catalysts work with specific Career Communities and cultivate Newsletters with relevant opportunities. Please email us at careers@owu.edu and provide robust details for the posting and application process, and we will include it in our bi-weekly newsletters. Schedule an Employer Spotlight Tabling Visit + Career Connection invites employers to table in the Hamilton William Campus Center (HWCC) for free one day per month! Please complete the form below to request a lobby table from 11:30 a.m. to 1 p.m. on your selected day. EMPLOYER SPOTLIGHT REGISTRATION Coordinate an Information Session/On-Campus Engagement + Employers interested in on-campus recruiting opportunities are invited to schedule an on-campus recruiting date. Special arrangements for interviews can be arranged. We prefer to have advance notice of at least two-three weeks to allow time to properly publicize your visit to our students. In order to allow a variety of recruiters to come to campus, we can accommodate two recruiting visits per organization each semester. Information sessions and faculty connections (availability depending) can also be arranged. Information sessions usually take place in the evenings or at noon. If you plan to conduct on-campus interviews, information sessions are frequently scheduled the day prior to raise visibility and general awareness of your organization. If an evening program or presentation is desired, please mention this option when you contact us. Please email careers@owu.edu with questions and to schedule a visit! Become an Employer Partner! + Did you know that OWU runs a robust Employer Partners program with 15+ employers? Our Employer Partners serve as a focus group for Career Connection, offering valuable insights and suggestions. These employers are featured to our students and invited to specialty events. Employer Partners are asked to attend at least one focus group meeting, and to engage at least twice with OWU students on campus via career fairs, tabling, networking, information sessions, or other programming. To become an Employer Partner, please complete the Employer Partners On-boarding Form Here and we will be in touch. Please see our current Employer Partners here . *Note that on-boarding occurs only in July & December* Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
    },
    "https://careers.owu.edu/channels/entrepreneurship/": {
      "title": "Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Entrepreneurship - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Entrepreneurship Are you looking for a career that will enable you to serve others and address tough social problems? In this career community, you can explore opportunities in Law & Social Justice, Human & Social Services, Social Entrepreneurship, Nonprofits, Government, and International Affairs & Public Policy. Entrepreneurship Careers Can Look Like Anything! Here Are Some of Our DEC Member’s Careers! Small Business Owner Data Analysts Research and Development CleanTech Founder Non-Profit Founder New Technology Discovery Ohio Wesleyan University Delaware Entrepreneurial Center (DEC OWU) DEC OWU is a first-of-its-kind collaboration among Ohio Wesleyan, Delaware County, and the City of Delaware, creating an entrepreneurial ecosystem and education center that develops the mindset and knowledge base focused on creating unique solutions to problems and opportunities that change the world. For more information about becoming involved in DEC OWU activities, please see its web pages . Delaware Does Entrepreneurship + Delaware Does Entrepreneurship provides entrepreneurs an opportunity to pitch their business ideas to a group of 50+ fellow entrepreneurs, students, potential investors, financial institutions, and business resource providers. You’ll also meet Delaware and Columbus leaders and resources. This is about building the entrepreneurial ecosystem! **Breakfast and coffee provided! Are you interested in pitching at an upcoming Delaware Does event? Contact Steve Flaherty to share your idea and learn more. + + Seeking Alumni in Entrepreneurship? Look no further! We have a cultivated list of Alums who are eager to speak with you. Check out their profiles and reach out to them! Access tools on our Build a Network page for further templates and resources! ENTREPRENEURSHIP ALUMNI PARTNERS We strongly encourage that you create a LinkedIn profile ! This is a great way to build your network and connect with fellow Alumni, faculty, and connections from OWU. Check out 15,000+ OWU Alumni , and join the OWU group below! OWU ALUMNI & FRIENDS GROUP Search JOIN THIS CAREER COMMUNITY! SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT Upcoming Events Alumni Partner Meet & Greet – The Art of the Informational Interview (Thursday, September 10th 2026, 7:00 pm – 8:00 pm EDT) July 8, 2026 Featured Internships CEO Office Operations Coordinator at Bites.com Inc. August 20, 2026 Entrepreneurship Internships Abroad – Presciant via The Intern Group at The Intern Group July 14, 2026 Executive Assistant at Poseidon Holdings June 19, 2026 OWU Alumni Partners SJ Barakony ’98 Entrepreneurial polymath (THE Education SHERpa ; H7 Network – frac CIO/CDO; startup champion; futurist) Avi Biswas ’14 Content Copywriter Avi Biswas Content Services Diana Roach ’72 Senior Director Volunteer Program (retired) – ACDI/VOCA Mark Shipps ’70 Environmental Services (Retired) Kyle Sjarif ’11 Product Manager – CarMax Career Resources & Job Boards Student Assistantship Program (StAP) Discover on-campus paid internships. Legacy Internships Discover on-campus paid internships for Legacy Students. First Gen Internship Discover on-campus paid internships for First Gen Students. NACE Competency Self-Assessment Are you career-ready? Discover more through this self-assessment tool. Exploratory Guide Exploratory Guide OWU Career Connection Overview Brochure/ Guide An introduction to OWU’s most important resource- Career Connection! 1 2 3 4 >> OWU Student Organizations The Entrepreneurship Club (Sorry, there’s no description of this club on Engage!) Women in Entrepreneurship The purpose of Women in Entrepreneurship (WIE) at Ohio Wesleyan University is to cultivate a supportive and inclusive environment that encourages and empowers students, especially women, to explore, engage with, and excel in the field of entrepreneurship. The organization aims to demystify the entrepreneurial journey, providing resources, knowledge, and networking opportunities that foster innovation, leadership, ... Featured Jobs An error has occurred, which probably means the feed is down. Try again later. Featured Internships CEO Office Operations Coordinator at Bites.com Inc. August 20, 2026 Employer: Bites.com Inc. Expires: 09/20/2026 CEO Office Operations & Project CoordinatorBites.com and Uniqueorn PX are seeking a highly organized and proactive coordinator to work directly with the CEO and keep priorities moving across technology, client operations, design, and construction.ResponsibilitiesTurn meetings […] Entrepreneurship Internships Abroad – Presciant via The Intern Group at The Intern Group July 14, 2026 Employer: The Intern Group Expires: 07/13/2027 Join The Intern Group's international Entrepreneurship internship program and interview with carefully selected host organizations including Presciant – a global brand consultancy that helps businesses use strategy, research, innovation and creativity to drive growth […] Executive Assistant at Poseidon Holdings June 19, 2026 Employer: Poseidon Holdings Expires: 09/30/2026 Job Title: Executive Assistant to the CEOCompany: Poseidon HoldingsLocation: RemoteAbout Poseidon Holdings:Poseidon Holdings is a dynamic, forward-thinking record label committed to nurturing musical talent and driving innovation within the industry. Additionally, we operate a public […] Gain Experience Greif Internships & Early Career Development 📍Delaware, OH, United States\n\n\n\nSponsor: Greif\n\n\n\n\nApply by: Oct 1, 2026\n\n\n\nAt Greif, we understand the value of cultivating a pipeline of talented individuals at the beginning of their professional journey. As such, Greif facilitates a number of Early Career programs to encourage growth & development through our Internship & Co-Op opportunities. Our Early Career Program in the ... Summer on the Cuyahoga (SOTC) 📍OH, United States\n\n\n\nSponsor: Summer on the Cuyahoga \n\n\n\n\nApply by: Nov 1, 2026\n\n\n\nUnforgettable Summer Internship Experiences are Made in Cleveland!\n\n\nSummer on the Cuyahoga (SOTC) connects young talent with professional opportunities in Northeast Ohio. The program immerses 70-80 students in the Cleveland area, in challenging internships with over 40 employers in a wide variety ... Ohio Department of Natural Resources Summer Internships 📍OH, United States\n\n\n\nSponsor: Ohio Department of Natural Resources\n\n\n\n\nApply by: Nov 1, 2026\n\n\n\nODNR offers hands-on, mission-driven summer internships across Ohio, giving students the chance to explore careers in conservation, science, education, law enforcement, communications, and more. Interns play a direct role in protecting Ohio’s natural resources — including forests, rivers, wildlife, and geological features — while ... Professional Associations Free One-Page Website Check out a resource for a free one-page website. Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
