    "https://careers.owu.edu/": {
      "title": "Home Page",
      "description": "Home Page - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Welcome to YOUR Career Resource Hub! Looking to launch a fulfilling career? OWU Career Connection is here to help! At OWU, America’s University for Ambitious Self Discovery, you will use our innovative “ Discover-Prepare-Launch ” model (rooted in Design Thinking) . The Career Connection team will guide you through exploring meaningful opportunities and designing a unique path forward. Our mission is to equip you with the skills to make informed career choices, develop essential competencies, and confidently navigate your future. You’ll graduate empowered to DESIGN your own SUCCESS! Your career journey is supported 24/7 through this comprehensive website, a central hub for resources, guides, job listings, and events. Career Connection helps you successfully prepare now for the career goals of your future. See below for how we can support YOU and please join Handshake as a pivotal first step to get started! Handshake is our featured resource for searching jobs and internships, finding events, and scheduling appointments with Career Catalysts . JOIN HANDSHAKE Students, Start Here! DISCOVER PREPARE LAUNCH Start where YOU are. Use assessments & tools for exploration. Learn what makes you stand out and discover future routes forward. Become a designer of your life and integrate your insights. Conduct exploratory conversations and build multiple paths forward. Set GROWTH goals and determine skill/training gaps (e.g. resumes, interviewing). Network with professionals and say YES to exciting opportunities. What is a Career Community? At Ohio Wesleyan University our eight Career Communities are organized by industry, not major, and offer ways for you to explore curated resources and learn about different career pathways. Please click on a logo below to explore the career community! VIEW ALL Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
    },
    "https://careers.owu.edu/resources/": {
      "title": "Resources Archives",
