nterviewing Assignment OWU Alumni Partners are available for informational interviews and offer a great opportunity for students to learn about career ﬁelds, build their network, and gain professional knowledge. Assignment learning goals: Resources Career Fair/Networking Assignment Attending events like Career Fairs and the Speed Mock Interview offers students valuable opportunities to explore career options, develop professional networking skills, and practice interviewing. Assignment Learning Goals Resources Transferrable Skills Assignment Through this transferable skills assignment, we remind students of the importance of not only the content they have covered but also the intellectual muscles they have developed—and are continuing to hone—as they engage with the course material in a variety… Resources Student Assistantship Program (StAP) Discover on-campus paid internships. Resources Legacy Internships Discover on-campus paid internships for Legacy Students. Resources First Gen Internship Discover on-campus paid internships for First Gen Students. 1 2 3 4 … 11 Next Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
