    "https://careers.owu.edu/resources/bishop-launch-program/": {
      "title": "Bishop Launch Program",
      "description": "Bishop Launch Program - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Bishop Launch Program Confident. Competent. Competitive. Now in its’ 9th year, the Bishop Launch Program (BLP) helps students become confident, competent, and competitive internship and job seekers. A semester-long program offered only during the fall term, BLP targets Sophomores & Juniors, (2nd and 3rd years) helps them professionalize their internship/job search process, and gives them the tools (acquired through a wide variety of workshops) to successfully launch into their careers post OWU. Over 70% of students who register to participate successfully complete BLP and earn a Professional Dress Award. (Note: BLP is not open to 1st year students.) Why Participate? + In addition to intensive support from Career Connection, each participant will be partnered with a specific career coach and receive further 1:1 support. BLP offers workshops focused on personal & professional development, intensive assistance on resume and interview skills, and an opportunity to engage with employers. We work closely with students to help them meet the program’s requirements while managing their busy academic/extracurricular schedules. Upon the successful completion of BLP, students receive a $200 Professional Dress Award . BLP is also a good resume builder; students are given language to add it to their resumes. Requirements for Completion + Participants will Attend a mandatory in-person or virtual BLP Info Session offered in the Spring and in August Take the Strengths Finder and have a conversation to understand the results Attend the virtual BLP Kickoff Event to learn about Power Skills and engage in conversations with employers & Alumni in small break-out groups Come to a Career Fair or 1 Employer Engagement event Attend 1 Networking workshop Attend 1 Professional Communication workshop Choose your o w n Professional Development Career Workshop (e.g. Get LinkedIn, Virtual Interviewing) Meet at least two times with your designated Career Coach (virtually or in-person) over the course of the semester and complete a Recorded Mock Interview and a Resume that gets approved. Reflections from BLP Participants + “I would definitely recommend BLP to a friend. It helped me to prepare for my career and to go through the interview process to get an internship. The BLP program was very manageable to do and was beneficial for me.” “I enjoyed going to all of the different personal meetings with my career coach and also getting to go to the different events. I liked that I could personalize the experience and make it fit my schedule.” “I would recommend BLP to other students because it gives you the opportunity to grow in professional development, and be able to experience direct career coaching. It also allows you to get difficult questions answered through personalized meetings.” Contact Mindy Agin , Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration for more information. Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
    },
    "https://careers.owu.edu/resources/harness-the-power-of-you/": {
      "title": "Career Clarity & Strategy Group",
      "description": "Career Clarity & Strategy Group - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Career Clarity & Strategy Group A 5-week Career Exploration Program Student Testimonials “I learned that my interests in sports, leadership, and helping others are important parts of my goals. Yes, the insights helped me think more clearly about realistic goals for my future career. –D. Ntwari ’28 “My Wandering Map helped me understand myself better and what was important to me. I realized my interests and was able to identify challenges that I want to tackle such as improving green infrastructure. I want to improve the environment while also helping people.” – H. Wagner ’28 Is this Right for You? + Feeling stuck, overwhelmed, or a bit clueless when it comes to thinking about careers or majors? Do you get anxious when asked “if you choose that major, what are you going to do with it?” If you’ve answered “yes” to one or more of these questions, consider registering for “Career Clarity and Strategy” – a 5 week career exploration program offered during Spring semester and facilitated by Mindy Agin, Assistant Director of Career Planning and Exploration. Further Details + Career Clarity and Strategy meets weekly from 12-1 (lunch provided) over the course of 5 weeks. You will develop wandering maps, hear professionals discuss their career journeys (e.g. when their majors did not sound like job titles), de-stress the career fair experience, and identify personal motivators and set goals . Benefits of Participating in Career Clarity and Strategy + At the end of 5 weeks, students will: Discover new, empowering information about themselves and their strengths and how to articulate it to others Gain a better sense of focus and direction Begin to identify transferable skills that come from different majors and can expand career options Create achievable goals to move forward with confidence Contact Mindy Agin for more information. Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
    },
    "https://careers.owu.edu/resources/career-readiness-course/": {
      "title": "Career Readiness Course",
      "description": "Career Readiness Course - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Career Readiness Course UC 154: 0.25 Credit Career Course, Fall Semester. The Career Readiness course offers a well-paved roadmap to success where you’ll be strategically connected with an Alumni Mentor who will offer relevant advice and suggestions throughout the duration of the course. This career course offers you a UNIQUE opportunity to get CREDIT for moving towards your career goals! Leigh Mascolino & Mindy Agin from the Career Connection team will offer individualized support to help you: Why Take This Course? + Get paired with an Alumni Mentor! Receive a free copy of the “Who Moved My Cheese” Book Gain skills to navigate change Identify a professional brand Articulate your career competencies Target your resume/cover letter/personal statement to opportunities Get into the employer mindset So much more! Who This Course is For + This course is best geared for Junior & Senior students Anyone looking to professionally prepare for life after OWU! Student Testimonials + “I learned a ton and it was a great experience overall!” “ Course offers information no other class on campus does and is a gateway to the career connection office.” “I expected to build confidence around my resume, interviews, and networking. I learned all of those things and more!” “It is a great course to help prepare students for the upcoming life after graduation. The exercises, materials and interaction in this course are all very helpful in helping students gain a better view of what the professional world looks like so that they can quickly adapt.” “I learned how to overcome fears of change and adaptability insights from the instructors and from my mentor.” “ “I almost dropped this course before the first day of class because I didn’t think it would be useful but it was! I liked the lessons for the most part and it is manageable to do alongside your other classes.” “ I think that this course really prepares students in various ways to navigate their next steps and advice and resources that are available to students. I think that the topics covered were very relevant and important. I also really liked the various modes of presenting the material. “ For more information and to see the syllabus please contact Leigh Mascolino or Mindy Agin in Career Connection. We are happy to share further details. SEE SYLLABUS HERE Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
    },
    "https://careers.owu.edu/resources/designing-your-future-course/": {
      "title": "Designing Your Future Course",
      "description": "Designing Your Future Course - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Designing Your Future Course UC 153: 0.25 Credit Career Course, Spring Semester. Based on the process known as “design thinking”, this course will challenge students to think of themselves as designers. In this class, students will have ideas, test them, and refine them over time to identify options to pursue following graduation. Through this course, you will learn how to DESIGN your career and IDENTIFY options to pursue following graduation. You will also complete a shadowing/informational interview opportunity! Leigh Mascolino & Mindy Agin from the Career Connection team will offer individualized support to help you: Why take this course? + Refine your career goals using Design Thinking principles Complete a robust shadowing/informational interview experience Come away with a revised resume and a LinkedIn Profile Gain further insights on your strengths, interests, and goals Learn fundamentals for interviewing and career/program preparation Receive individualized support from Career Connection! Who This Course is For + All years welcome: (MANY First Year students, Seniors, and everyone in-between has taken the course)! Anyone unsure about their career path and looking for hands-on support in exploring options Student Testimonials + “I expected to understand what I wanted to do after college better. I did and have gotten an internship in a field related to my major.” “This class is great for students who aren’t really sure what they want to do yet or who don’t often use Career Connection. It’s a great way to gain insight and connections.” “Before the course I was looking at my career very narrowly. After the course I changed the perspectives of my goals, I mean now I am considering several paths to get to my final destination/career.” “All of the assignments, like a resume and prototyping, are things I wanted to do but because it was an assignment it made me more inclined to do them, which I really liked. “This is a great course for students who are looking to improve their professional look by writing a resume, being able to interview well, along with other things. I recommend this to everyone because they are things that every student should work through and learn during their college experienc e.” For more information, please contact Leigh Mascolino ( lemascolin@owu.edu ) or Mindy Agin ( mbagin@owu.edu ) in Career Connection. We hope you’ll join us for this exciting opportunity to receive credit for solidifying your career goals! SEE SYLLABUS HERE! Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
    },
