    "https://careers.owu.edu/resources/real-life-101/": {
      "title": "Real Life 101",
      "description": "Real Life 101 - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Real Life 101 Getting ready to graduate? This can be both an exciting and overwhelming time in your life. Now in its 6th year, the Real Life 101 Program helps students about to graduate gain essential skills on how to network, balance finances, search for jobs, develop coping strategies, and succeed as an emerging professional. Students will come away with exceptional resources, Alumni connections, an “approved” resume, and OWU swag. This exclusive program is for motivated senior students who are eager to work closely with a mentor and prepare for the “real life” after college! Why Participate? Work with an Alumni Mentor in your field of interest Create a plan with your Career Catalyst & get your Resume approved Graduate with special Graduation Cords & Business Cards/Holders Participate in Professional Workshops on topics such as Job Search Strategies, Personal Finance, Finding Friends, Housing, etc. (you choose your own adventure!) Contact Leigh Mascolino and Mindy Agin for more information. Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
    },
    "https://careers.owu.edu/resources/workplace-readiness-certificate/": {
      "title": "Workplace Readiness Certificate",
      "description": "Workplace Readiness Certificate - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Workplace Readiness Certificate OWU is preparing students for the workplace – and that begins with your work on campus! Career Connection, as part of the Student Employment and Success Initiative (SESI), is excited to launch the Workplace Readiness Certificate . This certificate is required for all on-campus student workers, and will take approximately 1-2 hours to complete. This work should be done during paid hours, and does not need to be completed in one sitting. There is an accompanying Google Form that also needs to be completed. Students will be asked to complete The OWU Strengths Assessment and will be prompted with a link at the start of the course. To complete this course, you need to log in via Blackboard and find “Workplace Readiness Certificate” in the Organization Tab. Please see a preview of the Workplace Readiness Certificate Here. *Note that students should NOT take it this way, as this preview will not track certificate completion*. If you do not have access to the course in Blackboard, please email Leigh Mascolino to get added. Note that this only needs to be completed once during your time at OWU . Please work with your supervisor to take 1-2 hours to complete this certificate. Your supervisor will receive a copy of the Google Form that accompanies the course. Once the certificate is complete, we encourage students & supervisors to complete the below sheet! Questions? Please reach out to Leigh Mascolino, Director of Career Connection at lemascolin@owu.edu . Workplace Readiness Certificate Supervisor/Supervisee Reflection Sheet Additional Q/A below: Q. Is this mandatory? A. Yes, the University is asking that all student employees complete this certificate. Q. Does this need to be completed right away? A. We recommend that this is completed in your first month of employment this semester. You will continue to get reminders to complete it if it has not been completed. Q. What happens when the Certificate is completed? A. You will receive a certificate of completion and instructions on how to add this to your resume if desired. Your supervisor will also receive your responses. Q. Can non-student workers complete this? A. Absolutely! Please encourage any student to complete this certificate, it is open to all, but simply required for on-campus student workers. Q. Do I need to take this again if I get another job on campus? A. Nope! You only need to complete this certificate once, and then you are all set! Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
    },
    "https://careers.owu.edu/student-coaches-interns/": {
      "title": "Student Coaches/Interns",
      "description": "Student Coaches/Interns - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu Student Coaches/Interns Leigh Mascolino Carolyn Lammert Newton Kimberly ’13 Mindy Agin Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Contact 740-368-3150 Slocum Hall Room 211 lemascolin@owu.edu @leighmascolino SCHEDULE AND APPOINTMENT “To inspire confidence in others so that they can grow into their best selves and create a life fulfilled” Leigh oversees the Career Connection office, supervises staff, and provides strategic leadership in the OWU Career Connection program. She provides individualized career coaching to students and establishes rapport with staff, faculty, employers, and Alumni to expand job prospects and graduate/professional opportunities for OWU students. Leigh has a B.A. in Psychology from Ohio State and an M.S./Ed.S. in Career Counseling from Florida State, where she was trained under the Cognitive Information Processing (CIP) theory. She is a Certified Professional Career Coach (CPCC), a Certified Professional Resume Writer (CPRW), National Certified Counselor (NCC), a Certified Strengths Coach, and an MBTI Certified Practitioner. Leigh served as President of the Ohio Career Development Association and has most recently worked as the Manager of Career Services in the College of Pharmacy at Ohio State. ⬆ Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Contact 740-368-3549 Corns 230 ctlammer@owu.edu SCHEDULE AND APPOINTMENT Economics & Business Career Community To motivate, inspire and prepare students so that they can find joy, success and prosperity in their life’s work” As Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for the Economics and Business Department, Carolyn is responsible for educating students about career resources and connecting them to great internship and job opportunities with the ultimate goal of preparing them for life after OWU! Carolyn has a Bachelor’s Degree in Interpersonal and Public Communication from Bowling Green State University and a Master of Labor and Human Resources from The Ohio State University. She has a wealth of experience in multi-level corporate recruiting, student advising and internship program management. ⬆ Newton Kimberly ’13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & the Arts Contact 740 368-3642 Slocum Hall Room 208 nskimberly@owu.edu @newton-kimberly-iii SCHEDULE AND APPOITMENT Careers with Social Impact Career Community Humanities & Fine Arts Career Community Career Course Instructor “To lift others, support partners, and give people the tools in order to give them control” As a Career Catalyst (Careers with Social Impact), Newton works with students to help connect them to socially charged careers that align with their personal mission. Utilizing the amazing tools in the Career Connection office, Newton creates and maintains connections with students and employers to help ensure quality experiences for students, both pre and post-graduation, as well as quality and qualified candidates for employers. Newton has a Bachelor’s Degree in Sociology from Ohio Wesleyan University and a Master’s Degree in Public Administration from Cleveland State University.  Prior to returning to OWU, Newton worked as an Academic/College Advisor with I Know I Can and as the Development Associate for TECH CORPS. ⬆ Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
    },
    "https://careers.owu.edu/virtual-externships/": {
      "title": "How Forage Works",
      "description": "How Forage Works - Career Connection Skip to content No results Alumni Coach Referral Program Career Ambassadors Career Connection Team Channels Alumni & Friends Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Employers Entrepreneurship Exploratory Faculty & Staff Find a Job/Internship/Research Opportunity Graduate School Humanities and The Arts Interviewing Networking OWU Strengths Pre-Health STEM Write a Resume or Cover Letter Fairs and Events Grant Funds Home Page Resources Bishop Launch Program Career Clarity & Strategy Group Career Readiness Course Designing Your Future Course Impact Report Outcomes Data Real Life 101 Workplace Readiness Certificate Student Coaches/Interns Virtual Externships (Forage) ‹ OWU Homepage SUBMIT YOUR INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT IG IN Search Career Communities Careers with Social Impact Economics and Business Education Entrepreneurship Exploratory Humanities and The Arts Pre-Health STEM Programs Bishop Launch Program Real Life 101 Career Clarity & Strategy Group Designing Your Future Course Career Readiness Course Fairs and Events Career Preparation OWU Strengths Workplace Readiness Certificate Alumni Partners Resume & Cover Letters Job, Internship, Research Interviewing Networking Graduate School Virtual Externships (Forage) Grant Funds Our Team Career Connection Team Student Coaches/Interns Career Ambassadors Impact Report Outcomes Data Partnerships Faculty & Staff Employers Alumni & Friends Alumni Coach Referral Program Menu How Forage Works Forage – Virtual Externship Experiences For Your Resume! Participate in an online externship free of charge and build your resume and work on career goals! Students are taken through self-paced tasks that are designed to simulate the work of an intern or an employee at that organization. Each program takes 6 to 8 hours to complete and is completely free and done virtually ! Forage’s Virtual Experiences: Great Resume Builder! Forage provides free, short virtual work experiences designed by top companies. These online programs offer a taste of real-world career scenarios through a series of resources and tasks that simulate the day-to-day responsibilities of early career roles. Each experience lasts 6–8 hours and helps students develop relevant skills for their career journeys, all without an application process or any cost. Reasons to explore a virtual work experience with Forage include: Discovering potential career paths Building valuable skills and confidence for success Enhancing your resume with practical experience (see Forage’s referencing guidelines) How does Forage work? Students complete a series of tasks modeled after the real responsibilities of interns or new hires in their chosen fields. Each program, taking 6–8 hours, is free, self-paced, and open to everyone. See additional FAQ’s about Forage . Benefits of participating in Forage: Forage participants are twice as likely to be invited to interviews by employers. Employers are four times more likely to extend a job offer to Forage participants. Tasks reflect actual, day-to-day work at leading companies. Students gain access to curated resources for learning relevant industry skills. Video guidance from senior employees helps students learn directly from industry experts. Proceed to the OWU Forage Page and Sign Up Here Resource Categories and Career Communities # Virtual Externships (Forage) Meet the Team Leigh Mascolino Director of Career Connection Carolyn Lammert Assistant Director, Career Catalyst Program and Liaison for Economics and Business Newton Kimberly '13 Career Catalyst, Social Impact, Humanities & The Arts Mindy Agin Assistant Director of Career Planning & Exploration Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Drop-ins Daily : Monday & Wednesday :11:00 am 1:00pm; Tuesday & Thursday: 12-2pm Contact P 740-368-3152 E careers@owu.edu Location Slocum Hall 207 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 Ohio Wesleyan University 61 S. Sandusky St. Delaware, OH 43015 | 800-922-8953 | 740-368-3314"
    },
